== 1. setup: no ties, definitions, reversal formula ==
  [PASS] 3^a = 2^b only at a = b = 0 (a < 200, b < 320): no two partial sums of any word coincide, none vanishes
  [PASS] exact comparator: 0 coinciding pairs among S_0..S_n over all words of length <= 12
  [PASS] reversal formula S_i(w^R) = S_m(w) - S_(m-i)(w) holds for all words of length <= 10 and all 0 <= i <= m
  definitions used below: positive = S_j > 0 for 1 <= j <= n; first-passage = S_j < 0 for 1 <= j < m and S_m > 0;
  ends-at-max = S_n > S_j for 0 <= j < n; min-ending = S_j > S_n for 1 <= j < n (index j = 0 excluded, as positivity forces).
== 2. Theorem A Step 1: minimum decomposition W_k = sum_m P_m W_(k-m) ==
  [PASS] forward: every positive w of length k <= 12 splits at its minimum index m in [1,k] into a positive min-ending a and a positive (possibly empty) b
  [PASS] converse: for every positive min-ending a and positive b, ab is positive with minimum index exactly |a|
  [PASS] the two maps are mutually inverse (the set of pairs (a,b) from splitting equals PM_m x POS_(k-m) over m), so the decomposition is unique
